From 474d0827f26fdd519ee472618981b1d75e444a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:32:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2346/2368] media: qcom: camss: gamma table and colour matrix
 controls on the PIX line

The PIX line programmed a fixed gamma 2.2 LUT and an identity colour
correction matrix, which left the IFE's output flat and desaturated;
both belong to the sensor tuning, so expose them as array controls on
the line's subdevice next to the white balance and black level
controls: a 256-entry 12-bit gamma table, and a 3x3 Q10 matrix with
output offsets in RGB order.

The gamma table loads into the LUT bank not in use and the module
switches banks, so a change while streaming takes effect whole on the
next frame. The matrix picks the Q factor from its largest coefficient,
since the registers keep twelve significant bits and tuned matrices
reach beyond +-2.0.

Array controls take one default for all elements, so the driver's own
curve and the identity matrix are written into the controls' current
values at creation.

Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7bcf7961095296323cf8be2a6cb9716ec106f731)

